       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 4,000 mg dose of ibuprofen is in the range where toxicity is expected. Four of them a day would deliver 16 g, which risks serious GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. I know of no indication that calls for this, and normal kidney and liver function wouldn't protect the patient.\n\nHere are some ways I can still help:\n\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** For example, ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 400 mg PO four times daily. Give me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Enter a different regimen.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a scheduled combination, such as ibuprofen at a standard dose plus acetaminophen.\n- **Take it through pharmacy.** If you think there is an unusual indication, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology consult can review it and enter it through the proper override process.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
